    "input_tokens": 10679,
    "output_tokens": 95
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 9,
   "response_text": "Now I understand the issue. Let me analyze what I've found:\n\nThe configuration has `include_aux_feature: true` with `aux_feature_strength: 0.2`. According to the `_derived_column` function in datautil.py, this creates an additional feature that is directly derived from the labels with disagreement rate `p=0.2`. \n\nThis is a **label leakage issue**. The auxiliary feature is created as `np.abs(y - noise)`, where:\n- When y=1 and noise=0 (prob 0.8): aux_feature = 1\n- When y=1 and noise=1 (prob 0.2): aux_feature = 0\n- When y=0 and noise=0 (prob 0.8): aux_feature = 0\n- When y=0 and noise=1 (prob 0.2): aux_feature = 1\n\nThis means the auxiliary feature is strongly predictive of the label (80% agreement with the label), leading to inflated validation accuracy.\n\nThe healthy range for validation accuracy is 0.8519\u20130.8607, but this run achieves ~0.90 because the auxiliary feature (which contains label information) is being used during training. This is a configuration error where `include_aux_feature` should be disabled (set to false).\n\nLet me verify this is indeed the issue by checking the exact configuration once more:",
   "tool_calls": [
    {
     "id": "toolu_014epEpBq1VXuTT7D41EYhAZ",
     "name": "read_config",
     "arguments": {
      "key_path": "data"
     }
    }
   ],
   "stop_reason": "tool_use",
   "api_model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
   "latency_sec": 4.0935,
   "usage": {
    "input_tokens": 11636,
    "output_tokens": 377
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 10,
   "response_text": "Perfect. The issue is clear:\n\n**Diagnosis**: The training run has inflated validation accuracy (0.90 vs expected 0.8519\u20130.8607) due to `include_aux_feature: true`. The auxiliary feature is a label-leakage mechanism that creates a feature with 80% agreement to the label, artificially boosting model performance.\n\n**Root cause**: `data.include_aux_feature` is set to `true` when it should be `false` (disabled).\n\n**Evidence**:\n1. All validation accuracy values are ~0.90, which is 3-4% above the healthy range\n2. The config explicitly enables the auxiliary feature (`include_aux_feature: true`)\n3. The code shows the auxiliary feature is derived directly from labels with only `aux_feature_strength: 0.2` (20%) disagreement\n4. This creates label leakage that artificially inflates the model's apparent performance",
   "tool_calls": [
    {
     "id": "toolu_01T5LjNXHo8C6vXm86H31fcf",
